<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Asbestos roof removal in Geelong usually starts with something small. Someone goes up to clear the gutters, or a storm cracks a sheet, and the grey corrugated roofing on the house or the back shed suddenly looks like a problem. On a Geelong house that roofing is almost always Super Six or a similar asbestos cement profile, which was standard here from the mid-1940s through to the late 1980s.</p><p>Intact, it is non-friable, and that is the good news. The trouble starts when someone treats it like tin. We are not a removalist and we hold no licence. What we do is put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists working in the Barwon region, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on every quote they give you. You contract with them directly. Before any of that, the cheap and sensible first step is a sample: lab analysis runs $88 to $160 and settles the question in one to five business days.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Super Six and corrugated roofing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The grey asbestos cement profile on thousands of Geelong houses, garages and carports. It comes off in whole sheets rather than being broken up, which is the whole point of doing it properly.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Garage, shed and carport cladding</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Roof and wall sheeting on detached garages and backyard sheds, including the ones that have been leaning for a decade. If you want the concrete slab out as well, that is a separate line at $60 to $180 per square metre.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Eaves and soffit linings</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Small in area, but they sit right under the roofline and they get disturbed by roof plumbers, solar installers and anyone chasing a leak. A full set of eaves runs $1,500 to $2,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Test first, decide after</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A sample analysed at a NATA accredited laboratory costs $88 to $160. Most houses need three to eight samples, because the roof, the eaves and the shed wall are three different materials and each one is tested separately.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Class B licensed removalists</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Non-friable roof sheeting is Class B asbestos removal work. Every removalist we put you in touch with holds a current WorkSafe Victoria licence, and the number is printed on the quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Clearance and disposal sit with the licence holder</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">On a domestic job the licensed removalist has to obtain the clearance certificate, not you. The sheets go to a landfill authorised to receive asbestos, and in the Barwon region there is only one of those.</p>
      </div>
</div>
